    "title": "How to find a working endpoint",
    "step1Title": "1. Run a scan",
    "step1Text": "Choose the AmneziaWG protocol and the Standard preset. Click «Scan».",
    "step2Title": "2. Look at the nodes",
    "step2Text": "The table has a NODE column. These are Cloudflare datacenter codes: DME – Moscow, HEL – Helsinki, ARN – Stockholm, and others.",
    "step3Title": "3. Russian nodes are often blocked",
    "step3Text": "If endpoints through DME don't work with the services you need, exclude them:",
    "step3Item1": "«Exclude nodes» field",
    "step3Item2": "«Exclude countries» field",
    "step4Title": "4. Keep only what you need",
    "step4Text": "If you want specific nodes:",
    "step4Item1": "«Include nodes» field",
    "step4Item2": "«Include countries» field",
    "step5Title": "5. Configure scan parameters",
    "step5Text": "Open «Advanced options»:",
    "step5Item1": "how many addresses to check per subnet (more = slower but fuller)",
    "step5Item2": "set to 10 to see Tun Ping and Loss",
    "step5Item3": "speed test (slow but useful)",
    "step6Title": "6. Save the config",
    "step6Text": "Click the row with the best endpoint and press «Save selected». Or «Save best» for the fastest one.",
    "tipsTitle": "Useful tips",
    "tip1": "If standard ports are blocked, use «Port sweep» in the advanced panel.",
    "tip2": "If AmneziaWG doesn't get through, try MASQUE (TCP) – it often works where AWG is blocked.",
    "tip3": "If nothing is found, run «Find AWG junk» on the Tools tab."
